---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-notification-center</code> is the in-app inbox behind a bell: the bell shows the unread count,
  and pressing it opens a panel with the notifications, newest first, grouped under Today, Yesterday and
  dates, each with a relative time ("5 min. ago"). The panel has All and Unread filters, Mark all as
  read, and per-item buttons to mark read or unread and to dismiss. On phone-width screens it opens as a
  full-height side sheet.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; min-height: 4rem;'>
    <wc-notification-center id='inbox-demo' has-more></wc-notification-center>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var inbox = document.querySelector('#inbox-demo');
      var now = Date.now();
      var minute = 60000;
      var hour = 60 * minute;
      var day = 24 * hour;
      var page = 0;
      inbox.notifications = [
        { id: '1', title: 'Build failed', body: 'main #4521: 3 tests failed', timestamp: new Date(now - 5 * minute).toISOString(), intent: 'danger' },
        { id: '2', title: 'Ada Lovelace commented on "Q4 plan"', body: 'Looks good, one question about the budget.', timestamp: new Date(now - 2 * hour).toISOString(), avatar: 'https://peacock.redvars.com/assets/img/avatar.xs.webp' },
        { id: '3', title: 'Deployment finished', timestamp: new Date(now - day).toISOString(), intent: 'success', read: true },
        { id: '4', title: 'Storage almost full', body: '92% of 50 GB used', timestamp: new Date(now - 3 * day).toISOString(), intent: 'warning', href: '#storage' },
      ];
      function update(fn) {
        inbox.notifications = inbox.notifications.map(fn).filter(Boolean);
      }
      inbox.addEventListener('read-change', function (e) {
        update(function (n) {
          return e.detail.ids.indexOf(n.id) >= 0 ? Object.assign({}, n, { read: e.detail.read }) : n;
        });
      });
      inbox.addEventListener('dismiss', function (e) {
        update(function (n) {
          return n.id === e.detail.notification.id ? null : n;
        });
      });
      inbox.addEventListener('item-click', function (e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        myConsole.log('item-click: ' + e.detail.notification.title);
        update(function (n) {
          return n.id === e.detail.notification.id ? Object.assign({}, n, { read: true }) : n;
        });
      });
      inbox.addEventListener('load-more', function () {
        inbox.loading = true;
        setTimeout(function () {
          page += 1;
          inbox.notifications = inbox.notifications.concat([
            { id: 'old-' + page, title: 'Weekly summary', timestamp: new Date(now - (8 + page * 7) * day).toISOString(), read: true },
          ]);
          inbox.loading = false;
          inbox.hasMore = page < 2;
        }, 800);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>The app owns the data</h3>
<p>
  The component never changes <code>notifications</code>. It fires events and the app updates its data
  (optimistically if it likes) and assigns a new array:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <code>item-click</code> (<code>detail.notification</code>, cancelable): a notification was activated.
    One with <code>href</code> is a link and navigates unless the event is cancelled. Mark it read here if
    that is what your app wants.
  </li>
  <li>
    <code>read-change</code> (<code>detail.ids</code>, <code>detail.read</code>): from the per-item
    buttons and Mark all as read.
  </li>
  <li><code>dismiss</code> (<code>detail.notification</code>): from an item's dismiss button.</li>
  <li>
    <code>load-more</code>: from the Load more button, shown while <code>has-more</code> is set. Set
    <code>loading</code> while fetching.
  </li>
  <li><code>open</code> and <code>close</code> (<code>detail.reason</code>) for the panel.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Each notification is <code>{'{'} id, title, body?, timestamp, read?, intent?, href?, avatar? {'}'}</code>:
  <code>timestamp</code> is an ISO 8601 string, <code>intent</code> shows a colored icon when there is no
  <code>avatar</code> (an image URL). Dates and relative times use <code>Intl</code> in the resolved
  locale (<code>locale</code>, else the nearest <code>lang</code>).
</p>
